{
  "requirement": "The SDK presents node inputs using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\nIts text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet contents = domain.node_content(&node_id)?;\nlet text = contents.format();\n```\n\nLoading and fallible preparation occur in `Domain::node_content` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`. For inputs queued on an ask\nbuilder, these failures return `ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node`\ntool call, they are returned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue\nand recover.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `judge.rendering`.\n\n**1. Inputs are presented through `NodeContents::format`**\n- In `agent/tests.rs`, the test `Memory` domain keeps `Content` as a raw string plus a formatted string. Its `fingerprint()` returns the raw string and its `format()` returns the formatted one.\n- `validator_agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` sets the `distinct_pages` formatter and queues inputs through the `Question` criterion with `contents_of_current_node` or `contents_of_successors`. The `ParallelConversations` provider asserts that the first request already contains `ALPHA-CONTENTS` or `BETA-CONTENTS`. Those strings come only from `format()`; the fingerprint value is `source`.\n- A queued-input path that used the fingerprint or raw value instead of `format()` would fail that assertion.\n- `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` checks that the agent receives the formatted texts in queue order, with repeats.\n- `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer` checks that the text from `Domain::node_content` reaches the first user message in order.\n- `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` checks the `source` content in the first user message.\n- The `read_node` path is exercised by the same distinct-format `ParallelConversations` test.\n\n**2. Text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation**\n- `identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot` in `contracts.rs` reads a snapshot, then changes the underlying value. It asserts that `format()` still returns `before` and that the fingerprint matches the snapshot's. It also asserts that only one read occurred.\n- `validator_agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` asserts that the recorded dependency fingerprints match the snapshot content while the text delivered is the formatted text.\n- `domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement` in `src/sdk.rs` checks that formatting uses the supplied retained value without re-resolving the node.\n\n**3. Failures from `Domain::node_content`**\n- For queued inputs, `queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation` covers read failure, edge failure and a preparation failure. Preparation failure (`fail_prepare`) returns `ValidationError::Graph(\"render\")`. The test also asserts that no dependencies are recorded and that no agent request is made.\n- For `read_node`, `node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents` makes the formatter fail. It asserts that the tool result has `is_error`, the name `read_node` and the error text. It then asserts that the agent continues and submits, and that no dependency is recorded.\n\nI found no unaddressed obligation, and there are no acknowledgments to account for.",
  "references": "e7f4eb67f320fdbe3324029052cd29b2da4b151db0ea7c22bb85c62a7c32b9ac",
